:: The Bunker Intro
<<set $outside to 0>>
You climb down a long, dirty ladder before entering some sort of bunker.
<br><br>
<<getouticon "hole">><<link [[Next|Bunker]]>><<set $bunkerdepth to 0>><</link>>

:: Bunker
<<location "bunker">>
<<if $stress gte $stressmax and !$possessed>>
	<<passouttrash>>
<<else>>
	<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
	<<if $eventskip is 0>>
		<<rng>>
		<<if $rng gte 91>>
			<<eventbunkeritem>>
		<<elseif $danger gte (9900 - $allure) and ($settings.bestialityEnabled or $monster is 1)>>
			<<eventbunker>>
		<<else>>
			<<eventbunkersafe>>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $eventskip gte 1>>
		<<if $bunkerdepth is 10>>
			You are in the deepest part of the bunker you can go. Fettid water settles in the hallway blocking any deeper exploration. Strangely, there is a large sealed door with a pad seated to the side glowing in the darkness. Strange runes illuminate the surface of the pad, some kind of password?
		<<elseif $bunkerdepth lte 5>>
			You're in an abandoned bunker, the interior is dimly lit, and dust covers everything. As you glance over the walls of the bunker, you notice strange markings that seem to be in a language you've never seen before. The bunker seems to be in disrepair, and you wonder how long it's been since anyone has set foot here.
		<<else>>
			The deeper you go, the more deteriorated the the bunker becomes. There are pools of foul, stagnant water. Undoubtably the result of whatever leakage came from the landfill above.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<if $bunkerdepth is 10 and $codeEntered isnot "2863">>
			<<iconUi `"bunker-door.png"`>><<link [[Enter the lab|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>
			<br>
		<<elseif $bunkerdepth is 10>>
			<<iconUi `"bunker-door.png"`>><<link [[Inspect the keypad|Bunker Keypad]]>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $bunkerdepth lt 10>>
			<<walkicon>><<link [[Head deeper into the Bunker|Bunker]]>><<set $bunkerdepth += 1>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $bunkerdepth gt 0>>
			<<walkicon>><<link [[Head back toward the exit|Bunker]]>><<set $bunkerdepth -= 1>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $bunkerdepth is 0>>
			<<getouticon>><<link [[Exit the Bunker|Bunker Exit]]>><</link>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<set $eventskip to 0>>

:: Bunker Exit
<<set $outside to 1>>
You climb back up the dirty ladder before reaching the surface.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Trash]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Keypad
Before you lies a keypad with 8 distinct runes etched onto each surface. It seems to still be functioning but what could the password be?
<br><br>
<<set $codeEntered to "">>

<div class="keypad">
<<button "<<bunkericon1>>">><<set $codeEntered += "1">><</button>>
<<button "<<bunkericon2>>">><<set $codeEntered += "2">><</button>>
<<button "<<bunkericon3>>">><<set $codeEntered += "3">><</button>>
<<button "<<bunkericon4>>">><<set $codeEntered += "4">><</button>>
<<button "<<bunkericon5>>">><<set $codeEntered += "5">><</button>>
<<button "<<bunkericon6>>">><<set $codeEntered += "6">><</button>>
<<button "<<bunkericon7>>">><<set $codeEntered += "7">><</button>>
<<button "<<bunkericon8>>">><<set $codeEntered += "8">><</button>>
<<button "Clear">><<set $codeEntered to "">><</button>>
</div>
<br>
<<getinicon>><<link [[Input|BunkerCheck]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back|Bunker]]>><</link>>

:: BunkerCheck
The device falls silent for a moment as you wait. It sputters back to life before giving the result.
<br><br>
<<if $codeEntered is "2863">>
	The device chimes and the vacuum seal of the door hisses and opens into a new pristine looking room.
	<br><br>
	<<getinicon>><<link [[Enter|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	The device beeps and resets, seeming to have put in the wrong password. Maybe the library would have some information about these symbols?
	<br><br>
	<<getinicon>><<link [[Retry|Bunker Keypad]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back|Bunker]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Lab
You are in a perfectly preserved laboratory. Glass tubes contain specimens preserved in formalin. You can see shelves lined with different lurkers, large tubes containing strange creatures covered in tentacles, huge eggs in display cases, and mechanical devices lie scattered around the room.
<br><br>
<<iconUi `"lurker-vial.png"`>><<link [[Inspect the lurker vials|Bunker Vials]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<iconUi `"huge-tube.png"`>><<link [[Look into the huge tubes|Bunker Tubes]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<iconUi `"egg-case.png"`>><<link [[Read the display on the egg case|Bunker Eggs]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Check out the books lining the shelf|Bunker Shelf]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<iconUi `"mechanical-devices.gif"`>><<link [[Inspect the mechanical devices|Bunker Machines]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Bunker]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Vials
You walk up to the shelves and look closer at the femalin filled vials with the bodies of lurkers contained within. There is a surprisingly large variation of different types of lurkers, some white, some black, and even some purple.
<br><br>
Some of the vials seem broken and small shards cover the floor but you don't seem to see any danger or escaped lurkers. Where could they have gone?
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Tubes
Approaching the tubes you are faced with incomprehensible creatures. The tubes fill the complete height of the room and contain beasts constructed of tentacles. Cloven hooves and spindly legs hang under the bulbous tentacle covered body with a gaping snaggle toothed mouth.
<br><br>
You can barely stand looking at these creatures. It's time to go.
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Eggs
You approach a display case containing several thick shelled massive eggs. Each one stands over a foot tall and you can feel a heat eminating from behind the glass. Where and what are these eggs from?
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Read
Among the occult stories, you find an old faded journal. 
<br><br>
You pull down the journal and dust off the old leather cover, opening it to the first page. It reads, "Journal of Dr. Harper". You flip to the next page and begin to read, it seems many of the earlier pages have been torn out sometime a long time ago. "Entry 103: I have made a breakthrough in my recent studies. I began a search into the church and found some troubling discoveries. I've caught some bad wind of these so called Auriga and Virgo. I plan to continue my studies and attempt to uncover more."
<br><br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Continue to the next page|Bunker Read 2]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Put down the journal|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Read 2
The next page seems to be much later. The writing is more erratic and strange than before. It seems to be continuing from a missing previous page. "Entry 264: -or even something else. Modern archives of the old stories are all but wiped out but I find it hard to believe Abyssina and Auriga are born from the same cloth despite their many similarities. Similarly I believe that Auspacia shares a-" The page bares a tear that cuts off the rest of the page. Strange, was it the author or someone else?
<br><br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Continue to the next page|Bunker Read 3]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Put down the journal|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Read 3
By now, the writing is barely legible and the author's words are twisted. You're not even sure this journey could be considered a reliable source anymore. The final entry reads. "Entry 3485: This is it... this is the end. I have recieved a vision of the descent and blessing of Sezmis. This will inevitibly spell the end of mankind. I regret not seeing my family for all these years, my wife, my <<if V.NPCName[8].pronoun is "m">>son<<else>>daughter<</if>>. I am sorry." The page just ends. What happened? A lot of the names in this journal and the occult books along the wall are things you've never heard before. Unfortunately you've gleamed about as much as you could from this bookcase.
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Put down the journal|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Machines
You approach the various machines in the cluttered laboratory. There are sharp instruments, beds, and various other unrecognizable machines. Especially of note, a large six armed contraption over a medical bed, seeming to have been used for surgery.
<br><br>
<<if $prutiquest < 9 or $prutiquest is undefined or $lurkerinject is 1>>
	<span class="red">You currently do not have any modifications to apply at this time.</span>
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	<<iconUi `"mechanical-devices.gif"`>><<link [[Inject the modified lurker (1:00)|Bunker Lurker Inject]]>><<pass 60>><<set V.transformationParts.traits.lurker to "default">><<set $lurkerinject to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Lurker Inject
You place the vial of pale purple slime with the small orange egg inside into the arm of the machine and it whirs to life. You lie on the medical bed as the device pins you to place. Chemicals numb your senses as a scalpel gripped by a mechanical arm slices open your forearm. The vial's contents are ejected into a syringe arm which is pushed into the wound, releasing a sharp stream of ooze and egg into your arm. The machine then pinches the flesh together, sewing the skin back closed, and releasing you. 
<br><br>
Your arm aches but it surprisingly doesn't hurt too much. You wonder the true use for this machine and how much testing it would take to perfect something like this.
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Shelf
You near the bookshelf, pulling various dusty yet preserved books. Many of them are older esoteric manuals written in the old script. There are a couple old books of note.
<br><br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Pick up an old journal|Bunker Read]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Read an aged white faded book|Bunker Bog]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Look over a torn ancient green book|Bunker Fae]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Bog
The white book bears a yellow symbol on the cover and is coated in dust. You blow the cover and skim the book for important information.
<br><br>
"As the priest of the church, it has come to my attention there is a scourge of our religion hidden deep beyond the woods. They stem from our ilk yet claim worship of a false god. Be wary of these... dare I say cultists. Remain true to the faith of our church. Are you recording this? Scratch that from the record thi-"
<br><br>
The page ends there. It seems someone had rubbed out the imprint of these words from a blank page. After it had been discarded.
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Put down the book|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Fae
You pick up the green faded book, the writing is in an ancient language you cannot decipher. The text is torn and faded beyond your ability to read. Appended at the end, you find legible notes.
<br><br>
"Work toward deciphering the ancient text goes steady. The old Celtic would be simple enough to read without the irreprible fading and damage. From what I have found so far, this seems to be a book written in dedication to a goddess called "Auspacia" queen of the fae. The ancient rituals they cite involve partaking of some kind of primitive hallucinogen within a circle of mushrooms at the dead of night. I must say, these rituals seem quite primitive and unlikely, though since this very forest is the same forest of legend, I may test these findings."
<br><br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Continue to the next page|Bunker Fae 2]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Put down the book|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>

:: Bunker Fae 2
The note is more hastily written this time, due either to excitement or something else. 
<br><br>
The note begins, "This is truly unbelievable. At first I thought it was the hallucinogenics but I truly found myself within another realm. There existed beings that defied rational thought and have completely changed my understanding of our reality. I have procured eggs from the nest within the cave situated northeast of the entrypoint. These eggs shall reveal the truth in time, I am sure of it."
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Put down the book|Bunker Lab]]>><</link>>